msgstr "**Винаги включени модули** са съставени от `all.sh` и трябва да бъде източник на всичко, което се нуждае от стандартна среда на проекта (Python преводач, дистро по подразбиране, runtime контекст, инвентарни пътеки, GitHub маркери): `python.sh`, `runtime.sh`, `defaults.sh`, `inventory.sh`, `github.sh`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**An addon under the row role's `meta/addons/`.** Everything that needs an upstream plugin lives there, with its `mechanism` and, for an in-repo partner, a `bridges:` entry resolving to the service key it wires. The addon contract and its lints are requirement [026](026-unified-addon-syntax.md)."
msgstr "**A addon under the row's `meta/addons/`.** Всичко, което се нуждае от плъгин нагоре по веригата живее там, със своя `mechanism` и за партньор в комисията, `bridges:` влизане решаване на служебния ключ той жици. Договорът и мъховете му са задължителни. [026](026-unified-addon-syntax.md)."

msgid "**An agent can be provisioned with its own platform user account.** Creating an agent employee optionally provisions a dedicated identity through the platform's existing user mechanism (the `users` lookup, LDAP via [`svc-db-openldap`](../../roles/svc-db-openldap/), SSO via [`web-app-keycloak`](../../roles/web-app-keycloak/)); no new account system is built. The account is a **non-privileged standard user** by default (never administrator/service-account-with-mutating-tools). When enabled, the agent authenticates as its own user: OIDC login to its dashboard, a distinct mailbox/identity, and MCP calls made with `auth_subject: user` ([050](050-mcp-role-integration.md)) scoped to that account rather than a shared service account. The account is opt-in per agent; its password/token lives in the role's `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` block, never in README or env. An agent MUST also be deployable against an existing account (no forced account creation)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**An engine inside its consumer's project** — matrix with its own postgres, for instance — is started service by service rather than as a whole project, because bringing the project up would start the consumer and the chain refuses to replay while one runs. The discriminator is the dump's volume name against its project name: equal for the central engines (`postgres` in project `postgres`), different for a per-app one (`matrix_database` in project `matrix`)."
msgstr "**Двигател в потребителския си проект** . . . . . . . Дискриминаторът е името на обема на сметището срещу неговото име на проекта: равен на централния двигател (`postgres` в проект `postgres`), различна за една доза (`matrix_database` в проект `matrix`)."

