msgid "A role never names another role directly. It names a service key in its ``meta/services.yml``, and the key resolves to the role that provides it; an add-on under ``meta/addons/`` reaches the same provider by naming that key in its ``bridges:`` list. The two pages below list both sides for every ``web-app-*`` and ``web-svc-*`` role, regenerated from the roles on each build."
msgstr "Ролята никога не назовава друга директно. Назовава сервизен ключ. ``meta/services.yml``, и ключът решава за ролята, която го предоставя; допълнение в ``meta/addons/`` достига същия доставчик, като посочва този ключ в своя ``bridges:`` списък. Двете страници по-долу са изброени двете страни за всеки ``web-app-*`` както и ``web-svc-*`` роля, регенерирана от ролите на всяка сграда."

msgid "A role never reads the global modes `DEBUG` or `VALIDATE` from [01_modes.yml](../../../../../group_vars/all/01_modes.yml) itself. Its code calls `lookup('debug')` or `lookup('validate')` instead. The lookup resolves the role from `application_id`, reads `services.<entity>.<switch>.enabled` of the role's primary entity, and falls back to the global mode when that key is unset. It always returns a real boolean, so a string extra-var such as `-e DEBUG=false` stays false. A role without `application_id`, and any file that runs in another role's context (handlers, `meta/addons/`, tasks included by other roles), names the role literally: `lookup('debug', 'sys-svc-sshd')`."
msgstr ""

msgid "A role offers at most two modes in practice — swarm needs its own stack, host needs the absence of one — so a row flips between its two modes on consecutive sweeps. The network turns on `sweep // 2` so it does not flip in lockstep: a row with two modes and two network modes walks all four combinations over four sweeps instead of only two. Distro and filesystem read the position like an odometer, the distro as the low digit, so consecutive rows walk every pairing of the two pools rather than a diagonal through it. Turning both on the position directly would cover only as many pairings as the pools are long whenever they happen to be the same length, and no sweep would unlock that, because the sweep shifts both by the same amount. The architecture rotates on the position directly rather than as a third odometer digit. Two values are coprime with both five distros and the fifteen distro/filesystem positions, so walking it fastest still reaches every pairing, while making it the slowest digit would hand a role with few rows one architecture forever - and the point of the axis is that a role's own variants split over both. Priority rows skip the mode/network rotation entirely and take the whole cross-product at once; their distro, filesystem and architecture walk on across those combinations, so one priority role proves several distributions in one sweep."
msgstr ""

