msgid "Grafana runs one container per network the role is served on (``network_instances``): ``grafana`` for the canonical network and ``grafana-onion`` for the onion sibling. Grafana builds its OAuth callback and its links from the one ``root_url`` of its process, so each instance gets the root URL, domain, sign-out target and cookie flag of its network as container environment, and ``templates/proxy.conf.j2`` routes each vhost to the instance of its network. Each instance keeps its SQLite database on its own node-local volume (``grafana_data``, ``grafana_data_onion``; ``nfs: false``, ``placement: manager``); the entity declares ``backup.stop_required: true``, so the backup stops them before copying the databases. Both instances evaluate the provisioned alert rule, and the Alertmanager merges the identical alerts."
