msgid "The Actions Worker dies silently on ENOSPC while writing its own logs, so a full disk truncates the job without diagnostics; terminating the step at DISK_FLOOR_MB keeps enough room for rescue artifacts and the log upload. A stuck mount produces the same silence without touching either floor, so IO_STALL_CEILING_PCT ends the step while the runner can still upload. It takes three things together, because the pressure reading alone cannot tell a wedge from a busy disk and is not even this step's: a task in D state on the same sample, WEDGE_SAMPLES breaches in a row, and a step old enough to own a whole STALL_WINDOW_S of the trailing average. Without the last one an I/O-heavy predecessor aborts its successor before that step has issued a single read."
msgstr ""

msgid "The Actions worker writes its own diagnostics log to `/`. When `/` runs full the worker dies, the job log is lost and no `always()` step runs ([#1377](https://github.com/infinito-nexus/core/issues/1377)). The image build therefore runs under [disk/guard.sh](../../../../../scripts/github/runner/disk/guard.sh):"
