# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The flag is mandatory, enforced by [test_onion_port_flag.py](../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_onion_port_flag.py): every category declared under `local` or `public` needs a `true` or a `false`, and every `false` needs `# nocheck: onion-flag` plus the reason it is false. Four groups are settled centrally instead and take no flag: the categories a hidden service cannot carry (`relay`, `media`, `stun_turn`, `stun_turn_tls`), the proxy-fronted `http`, `sso` and `websocket`, the implicit-TLS variants (`smtps`, `imaps`, `pop3s`, `ldaps`), and any entity that already answers the question through `exposed:`."
msgstr "Флагът е задължителен, приложен от [test_onion_port_flag.py](../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_onion_port_flag.py): всяка категория, декларирана в `local` или `public` се нуждае от `true` или `false`, и всеки `false` нужди `# nocheck: onion-flag` Плюс причината да е лъжа. Четири групи се уреждат централно и не вземат флаг: категориите, които една скрита услуга не може да носи (`relay`, `media`, `stun_turn`, `stun_turn_tls`), прокси-преден `http`, `sso` както и `websocket`, имплицитните варианти TLS (`smtps`, `imaps`, `pop3s`, `ldaps`), и всеки субект, който вече отговаря на въпроса чрез `exposed:`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The flavor enum is ``{oidc, oauth2, saml}`` with ``oidc`` as the default when omitted. The ``is_proxy_gated`` predicate is the one place that encodes \"the oauth2-proxy sidecar fronts this role\" — every other layer MUST consult this helper instead of re-implementing the ``enabled AND flavor == 'oauth2'`` compound. The ``oauth2_*`` keys expose the gated upstream config so call sites resolve cross-role data through one named property rather than a literal ``lookup('config', app_id, 'services.sso.oauth2.<sub>')`` (which would otherwise trip the literal-protocol-lookup and lookup-config-path static-scan guards)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The fleet is deployed on **every** cluster node, but not as a ``docker stack`` service (``compose_mode_force: compose`` in ``vars/main.yml``): each runner needs the docker socket and the registered identity of exactly its node. The image is built once on the manager and distributed through the registry dependency (``svc-registry-docker``), the only part that runs as a swarm service."
msgstr ""

msgid "The fleet is deployed on **every** cluster node, but not as a `docker stack` service (`compose_mode_force: compose` in `vars/main.yml`): each runner needs the docker socket and the registered identity of exactly its node. The image is built once on the manager and distributed through the registry dependency (`svc-registry-docker`), the only part that runs as a swarm service."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The floor is the one :func:`reason` applies to a plain echo, because the risk it guards against is the same: a short source legitimately survives inside a longer rendering, a sentence does not."
msgstr "Подът е този. :func:`reason` се прилага за обикновено ехо, защото рискът, срещу който се пази, е същият: кратък източник легитимно оцелява вътре в по-дълго представяне, изречение не."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The floor keeps a short entry out: ``Situation`` becomes ``Lage`` and loses half its characters while saying the same thing. A passage past it that comes back halved has dropped a clause."
msgstr "Подът има кратък вход: ``Situation`` става ``Lage`` и губи половината си герои докато казва същото. Проход покрай него, който се връща наполовина е спаднал с клауза."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The focus here is not feature work, but control and safety: development workflows sometimes need a softer security posture, while cleanup paths must leave the system in a predictable state again. That makes this area less about convenience and more about trust, reversibility, and clear operational boundaries. 🔒"
msgstr "Фокусът тук не е функция работа, а контрол и безопасност: работните потоци за развитие понякога се нуждаят от по-мека поза сигурност, докато пътищата за почистване трябва да напуснат системата отново в предсказуемо състояние. Това прави тази област по-малка за удобство и повече за доверие, обратимост и ясни оперативни граници. 🔒"

