msgid "[x] `create/relay.yml` takes absence only from an exact name in `network ls` (`:2-19`), inspects a present network in a block guarded by that fact (`:21-38`) and fails unless it is an `overlay` of scope `swarm`, attachable, encrypted exactly when `swarm.network.encryption` is on, on the pinned subnet and in the provider's stack namespace (`:40-54`). Neither probe tolerates a failure. It creates the network with `--subnet`, the `com.docker.compose.network`, `com.docker.compose.project` and `com.docker.stack.namespace` labels, and `--opt encrypted=true` only when encryption is on (`:56-69`). Tested against mocked probes: absent, a name that only contains the relay name, matching, nine drifts, encryption off on both sides and on one side, and the probe tasks' failure handling (`test_network_relay_create.py`)."
