msgid "``PROTECTED`` claims every digit run and every bare markup character, because over-claiming is right when masking. As a comparison basis it is not: the translation is another language whose ordinary prose trips those same rules, and a gained parenthesis breaks nothing the source carried. What does break something is an invented placeholder - an injected ``%s`` fails ``msgfmt``, a decoder artefact like ``♪`` or a leaked ``<unk>`` is garbage - so only those keep a surplus refused."
