msgstr "```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``sso.enabled``, ``logout.enabled`` and ``email.enabled`` to ``false``; the role serves a static single-page wheel with no accounts and no auth layer. There is nothing for the ``biber`` or ``administrator`` persona to log in to, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona и изходните твърдения за изпълнимост работят безусловно."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``sso.enabled``, ``logout.enabled`` and ``redis.enabled`` to ``false``; the upstream image is a client-side QR generator with no accounts and no server-side session. There is nothing for the ``biber`` or ``administrator`` persona to log in to, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline reachability assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``sso.enabled``, ``logout.enabled`` and ``redis.enabled`` to ``false``; the upstream image is a client-side QR generator with no accounts and no server-side session. There is nothing for the ``biber`` or ``administrator`` persona to log in to, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona и изходните твърдения за изпълнимост работят безусловно."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```plugins/lookup/email.py`` <../../plugins/lookup/email.py>`__ — the email abstraction"
msgstr "```plugins/lookup/email.py`` <../../plugins/lookup/email.py>` год."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```svc-ai-litellm`` <../svc-ai-litellm/>`__ publishes one routing alias. When this service is deployed, the gateway’s pre-call hook asks it which of the eligible models should answer, passing the prompt as the state and the surviving aliases as the options of a single ``choice`` question. ``services.litellm.router.strategy`` follows ``services.s1.enabled``, so deploying this role is what switches the gateway from a weighted score to a System One decision."
msgstr "```svc-ai-litellm`` <../svc-ai-litellm/>`__ publishes one routing alias. When this service is deployed, the gateway’s pre-call hook asks it which of the eligible models should answer, passing the prompt as the state and the surviving aliases as the options of a single ``choice`` question. ``services.litellm.router.strategy`` follows ``services.s1.enabled``Така че разполагането на тази роля е това, което превключва портала от среднопретеглена оценка към System One решение."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```sys-svc-mail`` <../sys-svc-mail/>`__ — how applications send mail"
msgstr "```sys-svc-mail`` <../sys-svc-mail/>` год."

msgid "```tasks/01_admin.yml`` <./tasks/01_admin.yml>`__ provisions only the administrator in Shopware’s user table. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``services.sso.flavor: oidc``, so no oauth2-proxy fronts the role and the storefront carries no authenticated surface at all; the Keycloak login provider that ```tasks/setup/oidc.yml`` <./tasks/setup/oidc.yml>`__ configures covers the administration backend alone. ``biber`` therefore has no storefront account in any matrix variant and ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` unconditionally. ```files/playwright/test-rbac.js`` <./files/playwright/test-rbac.js>`__ asserts that its backend sign-in through Keycloak is refused without a group and admitted with the ``Editor`` ACL role as a member of the ``editor`` group."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/01_setup.yml`` <./tasks/01_setup.yml>`__ seeds only the administrator into Magento’s admin table (``bin/magento setup:install --admin-user``, credentials from ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); ``biber`` reaches the backend solely through the oauth2-proxy declared in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that proxy is absent and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```tasks/01_setup.yml`` <./tasks/01_setup.yml>`__ seeds only the administrator into Magento’s admin table (``bin/magento setup:install --admin-user``, credentials from ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); ``biber`` reaches the backend solely through the oauth2-proxy declared in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that proxy is absent and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` и работи във всеки вариант."

msgid "```tasks/02_manager_ops/03_upgrade.yml`` <./tasks/02_manager_ops/03_upgrade.yml>`__ includes ```03_upgrade/01_post_upgrade.yml`` <./tasks/02_manager_ops/03_upgrade/01_post_upgrade.yml>`__, the appstore app update and ``occ maintenance:repair --include-expensive``, only while the version ``occ status`` reports after ``occ upgrade`` differs from the one ``version.php`` declared before the deploy or from ``files/mimetype_version``, the server version the expensive repair last ran for. A fresh install, every upgrade path and a deploy that stopped before the repair run the pass, a redeploy of an unchanged version skips it."
msgstr ""

msgid "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account and converges its password to ``ADMIN_PASSWORD``, but the shared persona flow fills ``ADMIN_USERNAME`` into the native form while Mastodon’s ``/auth/sign_in`` only accepts the e-mail in ``user[email]``, so the journey cannot sign in natively; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>`__) drives the same admin journey and skips on the same flag."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/addons/AIEditingAssistant.yml`` <tasks/addons/AIEditingAssistant.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` and asserts the provider, the base URL and the model, so an unconfigured surface cannot reach a green deploy."
msgstr "```tasks/addons/AIEditingAssistant.yml`` <tasks/addons/AIEditingAssistant.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` и твърди доставчика, основния URL и модела, така че неконфигурирана повърхност не може да достигне зелено разполагане."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/addons/MachineTranslation.yml`` <tasks/addons/MachineTranslation.yml>`__ asserts the endpoint shape before the container is touched (plain ``http``, an undotted service name, the engine’s internal rather than published port), then reads the global back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` and asserts ``type`` and ``url``, so an extension that fell back to its upstream default cannot reach a green deploy."
msgstr "```tasks/addons/MachineTranslation.yml`` <tasks/addons/MachineTranslation.yml>`__ asserts the endpoint shape before the container is touched (plain ``http``, an undotted service name, the engine’s internal rather than published port), then reads the global back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` and asserts ``type`` and ``url``, така че удължаване, че падна обратно към своя нагоре по течението по подразбиране не може да достигне зелено разполагане."

